Sample YAML Configuration
YAML is used to define the app’s configuration, similar to how it’s used in Home Assistant () or DevOps blueprints (). Below is a sample blueprint.yaml for MyFamilyDynasty’s core structure, defining the app’s services and parameters.
apiVersion: myfamilydynasty/v1
kind: AppBlueprint
metadata:
  name: myfamilydynasty-core
  version: 1.0.0
spec:
  parameters:
    - name: AppName
      prompt: "Enter the name of the application"
      default: "MyFamilyDynasty"
    - name: DatabaseHost
      prompt: "Enter the database host"
      default: "localhost"
    - name: StorageBucket
      prompt: "Enter the cloud storage bucket name"
      type: SecretInput
    - name: MaxCollaborators
      prompt: "Maximum number of collaborators per tree"
      type: Integer
      default: 10
  services:
    - name: frontend
      type: ReactNative
      path: ./frontend
      config:
        platform: [ios, android, web]
        theme: 
          primaryColor: "#4682B4"
          secondaryColor: "#32CD32"
    - name: backend
      type: NodeJS
      path: ./backend
      config:
        port: 8080
        database: 
          type: MongoDB
          uri: !expr "DatabaseHost + '/myfamilydynasty'"
    - name: storage
      type: AWS_S3
      config:
        bucket: !expr "StorageBucket"
        region: us-east-1
    - name: auth
      type: OAuth2
      config:
        providers: [google, facebook, email]
  files:
    - path: config/app.yaml
      writeIf: !expr "AppName != ''"
    - path: secrets.xlvals
      writeIf: !expr "StorageBucket != ''"
      content: 
        bucket: !expr "StorageBucket"
  includeBefore:
    - blueprint: base/security
      parameterOverrides:
        - name: EncryptionLevel
          value: "AES-256"
